  7      21         3        9   12       4096        4096     9      512  OK
  8      28         4       12   16      65536      (skip)    12     4096  closed-form

  EXPONENT formula for Fix_anti(phi)_full:
    exponent = (#phi-orbits on the C(n,2) unordered vertex-pairs)
    Derivation: pairs split into (i) self-paired pairs {u, n+1-u}
    [phi swaps the two endpoints -> constraint is vacuous, 1 free bit]
    and (ii) free 2-orbits {p, phi(p)} [T on one determines the other,
    1 free bit]. So EVERY phi-orbit on pairs = exactly 1 free bit.

    n  C(n,2) exp=Fix_anti self=floor(n/2)  half(n)  exp-half  half+floor(n/2)
    3       3            2               1        1         1                2
    4       6            4               2        2         2                4
    5      10            6               2        4         2                6
    6      15            9               3        6         3                9
    7      21           12               3        9         3               12
    8      28           16               4       12         4               16
    9      36           20               4       16         4               20
   10      45           25               5       20         5               25
   11      55           30               5       25         5               30
   12      66           36               6       30         6               36

  RECONCILIATION (fixed-HP frame vs full frame), CORRECTED:
    full-frame exponent = half(n) + floor(n/2).
    Identity  exp == half(n)+floor(n/2)  for n=3..12:  True
    => Fix_anti(phi)_full = 2^half(n) * 2^floor(n/2).
    The extra +floor(n/2) (NOT n-1) is the number of phi-SELF-PAIRED
    vertex-pairs {u, n+1-u}: each carries 1 free bit because the anti-
    automorphism constraint on a self-paired pair is VACUOUS (phi swaps
    its two endpoints, so T(v,u)=T(v,u) is automatic). The fixed-HP frame
    PINS exactly these floor(n/2)... no: it pins the n-1 base-path arcs and
    leaves m=C(n-1,2) tile bits, of which 2^half are grid-sym. The clean
    statement is the COUNT identity exp = half + floor(n/2); the half-tiling
    (grid-sym) part is 2^half, the remaining 2^floor(n/2) lives on the
    self-paired (anti-diagonal) pairs that the half-tiling frame collapses.

[c] THE 2:1 FOLD (orbifold Q_m/rho): branch locus = grid-sym tilings
  n      2^m  #orbits #fixed(branch) #2-orbits(free)  (2^m+2^half)/2   OK
  3        2        2              2               0               2 OK
  4        8        6              4               2               6 OK
  5       64       40             16              24              40 OK
  6     1024      544             64             480             544 OK
  7    32768    16640            512           16128           16640 OK
    free tilings pair up (2-orbits); grid-sym tilings are the branch
    locus (fixed points of the involution).  Euler-orbifold style:
    #orbits = #2-orbits + #fixed = (2^m - 2^half)/2 + 2^half = (2^m+2^half)/2.

